#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1325 expect=violation domain=AE
#note "Mirrors rulespec PMDA-SD1325.yaml (the rule's only prior guard; PMDA twin of FDA-SD1325, byte-identical executable fields but a DIFFERENT corpus entry - a regeneration that dropped or mis-derived the PMDA copy leaves the FDA suite green and only this one red). Submitted dataset label 'AE' vs Define-XML description 'Adverse Events' -> one finding, pinned on both projected labels."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#define dataset-metadata AE name=AE label="Adverse Events"
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt dataset_label=AE define_dataset_label="Adverse Events"
dataset AE label="AE"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
---
S1 | AE | 001 | 1 | HEADACHE
